From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: HDMI FreeSync/VRR without an MCCS VCP code

7.4 (e4dca268eea6, "Restore FreeSync VCP code check for HDMI/PCON
sinks") clears freesync_capable for a native HDMI (TMDS) sink whose EDID
has no FreeSync MCCS VCP code. TVs have no MCCS: an LG B4 with FreeSync
Premium on sends the AMD VSDB 6d1a000002012878000000000000 (FreeSync,
40-120 Hz, VCP code 0), so amdgpu reported a VRR range of 40-120 and
vrr_capable 0. The same check also undoes 7.4's HDMI 2.1 VRR range
(HF-VSDB) fallback, which a sink without an AMD VSDB reaches with VCP
code 0 too. On 7.3.4 the VCP code was only looked at when MCCS was read
(do_mccs), so such TVs were VRR-capable there, and YBLOD's opt-in
FreeSync (Kodi's variable refresh rate) worked on them.

amdgpu.freesync_hdmi_vcp (default 0): 0, native HDMI does not need the
VCP code; 1, upstream's check. The PCON whitelist case and the MCCS
block (do_mccs) are upstream's either way: a sink with a VCP code that
MCCS says does not support FreeSync still loses it. HDMI FRL sinks are
not affected by the check upstream and are not changed here.

Nothing else on the HDMI path looks at the VCP code: with an AMD VSDB
that says FreeSync, amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_state_on_stream() sends
the FreeSync SPD packet (PACKET_TYPE_VRR, v1); without one, HDMI VRR's
VTEM. No KUnit test covers HDMI with an AMD VSDB and VCP code 0 (the
HDMI test has no VSDB and still expects no FreeSync).

From big-fella (linux-yblod 7.4rc2-2,
linux-9929-big-fella-amdgpu-hdmi-freesync-no-vcp.patch), unchanged: it
applies to YBLOD's 7.4-rc3 series at the same place, on a byte-identical
amdgpu_dm_connector.c. big-fella records the failure on ryzen-fella's LG
B4 (vrr_capable 0), not a run with this patch; it has not run on YBLOD.
---
 .../display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c   | 22 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
index 5aa71e456ca9..b2bd204ba351 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -3791,6 +3791,21 @@ STATIC_IFN_KUNIT int get_amd_vsdb(struct amdgpu_dm_connector *aconnector,
 }
 EXPORT_IF_KUNIT(get_amd_vsdb);
 
+/*
+ * big-fella: upstream (e4dca268eea6) reports a native HDMI sink without an
+ * EDID FreeSync VCP code (the AMD VSDB's MCCS VCP code) as not FreeSync
+ * capable. TVs have no MCCS: an LG B4 with FreeSync Premium on sends an AMD
+ * VSDB with FreeSync 40-120 Hz and VCP code 0, and its HDMI 2.1 VRR range
+ * (HF-VSDB) was thrown away by the same check. 0 (default): not required on
+ * native HDMI; 1: upstream's check. The PCON whitelist case and MCCS
+ * (do_mccs) are upstream's either way.
+ */
+static bool freesync_hdmi_vcp;
+module_param(freesync_hdmi_vcp, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(freesync_hdmi_vcp,
+	"Native HDMI FreeSync/VRR needs an EDID FreeSync MCCS VCP code, as upstream "
+	"(big-fella; default false: TVs have none; read at the next EDID update)");
+
 /**
  * amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps - Update Freesync capabilities
  *
@@ -3989,8 +4004,11 @@ void amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps(struct drm_connector *connector,
 			amdgpu_dm_connector->min_vfreq;
 	}
 
-	/* HDMI/PCON without an EDID FreeSync VCP code is not FreeSync-capable. */
-	if ((sink->sink_signal == SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_TYPE_A ||
+	/* HDMI/PCON without an EDID FreeSync VCP code is not FreeSync-capable.
+	 * big-fella: on native HDMI only with amdgpu.freesync_hdmi_vcp=1; TVs
+	 * have no MCCS and leave the AMD VSDB's VCP code 0.
+	 */
+	if (((sink->sink_signal == SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_TYPE_A && freesync_hdmi_vcp) ||
 	     as_type == FREESYNC_TYPE_PCON_IN_WHITELIST) &&
 	    !sink->edid_caps.freesync_vcp_code)
 		freesync_capable = false;
